---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Delete a Connect account"
  description="How to delete an mdbase Connect account and the collection data mdbase stores, including for TaskNotes users."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <h1>Delete a Connect account</h1>
    <p class="page-intro__lede">
      Permanently delete your mdbase Connect account and the collection data
      mdbase stores for it. These steps also apply if you use mdbase Connect
      through TaskNotes.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a
        class="button button--primary"
        href="https://editor.mdbase.dev/connect/account"
      >Open Connect account settings</a>
    </div>
  </header>
  <article class="legal">

    <h2>How to delete your account</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Open <a href="https://editor.mdbase.dev/connect/account"
          >Connect account settings</a
        > and sign in to the mdbase Connect account you want to delete. TaskNotes
        users should sign in with the Connect account linked to TaskNotes.
      </li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li>
      <li>Reauthenticate when prompted.</li>
      <li>
        Type <strong>DELETE</strong>, then confirm the permanent account deletion.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Data that is deleted</h2>
    <p>Deleting your mdbase Connect account permanently removes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your Connect account and sign-in methods.</li>
      <li>Browser sessions.</li>
      <li>
        Application access and grants, including access previously granted to
        TaskNotes.
      </li>
      <li>Registered devices.</li>
      <li>
        For collections you own, the data mdbase stores to sync them: the
        encrypted changes, snapshots, and attachments, and, for Cloud copy
        collections, the readable copy and mdbase’s copy of the collection key.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your membership in collections other people own. Those collections stay
        with their owners.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Access and control-plane state are removed immediately. Durable cleanup
      of stored collection data then continues automatically in the background.
    </p>

    <h2>Data that is not deleted or may be retained</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Collection folders on your own devices are not deleted. Each device that
        synced a collection keeps its copy as ordinary files. Delete those copies
        yourself if you no longer want them.
      </li>
      <li>
        People you shared a collection with keep the files they already had.
      </li>
      <li>
        Security or audit records necessary to document the deletion, prevent
        abuse, or meet legal obligations may remain. During the open beta,
        mdbase Connect does not promise a fixed retention period for these
        records.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Delete data without deleting your account</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete individual records or files, or delete individual
      collections, without deleting your mdbase Connect account. Use the
      relevant application or collection-management controls to remove only the
      data you choose.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
